---
// About, rebuilt 20 Nov 2026 on Jodie's Etsy template in the shared site style.
import TemplateLayout from "../layouts/TemplateLayout.astro";
import { library, community, weekendEcosystem, cap } from "../data/facts.js";
import { FEATURED } from "../we-reviews.js";

const SITE = "https://www.thedigitalincomeedit.com";

// What I learned. Founder lessons, stated once each, no villain required.
const lessons = [
  {
    t: "The offer decides everything downstream.",
    p: "A page, an email, a pin: each one is only as clear as the sentence it's selling. So the sentence comes first, before a single post exists.",
  },
  {
    t: "Reach is rented. Architecture is owned.",
    p: "Traffic arrives and leaves on someone else's schedule. A funnel on a domain you own keeps working on the Tuesday you skip.",
  },
  {
    t: "Faceless isn't the same as hidden.",
    p: "My real face is never required. The brand's face is an AI persona, and the business behind her is real, built and running.",
  },
  {
    t: "The channels are rooms, not the house.",
    p: "Pinterest, blogging, email and automation each have a place inside one build. None of them is the headline, and none of them is the whole business.",
  },
];

// Why the order matters: the method in four rooms.
const order = [
  { n: "01", name: "Offer", p: "What you sell, who pays for it and what it costs them. Decided on paper, first." },
  { n: "02", name: "Funnel", p: "The road a stranger walks from a free thing to a paid one: the page, the emails, the ask." },
  { n: "03", name: "Automation", p: `AI and schedules take the repeat work. One article becomes ${weekendEcosystem.assetsPerArticle} finished assets.` },
  { n: "04", name: "Audience", p: "Only now does the traffic switch on, pointed at a house that already knows what to do with a visitor." },
];

// What you can inspect. Every row is a live page on this site.
const inspect = [
  { room: "The library", t: "Every guide started as a lesson", p: `${cap(library.guidesWord)} step-by-step guides and ${library.articles} quick reads, each one a Skool lesson first, turned into a page by the method it teaches.`, href: "/learn", go: "Read a lesson" },
  { room: "The course", t: "The Weekend Ecosystem™, from the inside", p: `${weekendEcosystem.modules} modules, delivered as a live website on the very kind of site it teaches you to build. No email needed to look.`, href: weekendEcosystem.preview, go: "Take the free look" },
  { room: "The offer", t: "The One‑Sentence Offer tool", p: "Step one of the method, as a free tool. Type your offer as you say it now and watch it get checked. No email.", href: "/resources/one-sentence-offer", go: "Test your offer" },
  { room: "The funnel", t: "The Weekend Build Challenge", p: "Five free days by email that walk a stranger, in order, from a model to an offer to a way to be found.", href: "/resources/weekend-build-challenge", go: "Inspect the five days" },
  { room: "The email", t: "The Weekly Edit, every Sunday", p: "Written once a week and delivered by the automation underneath this site.", href: "/newsletter", go: "Read the letter" },
  { room: "The classroom", t: "The community behind it all", p: `Where women build the same business, lesson by lesson, beside each other.`, href: "/membership#room", go: "See the classroom" },
];

const schema = [
  {
    "@type": "Person",
    "@id": `${SITE}/about#founder`,
    name: "Jodie",
    jobTitle: "Founder",
    worksFor: { "@id": `${SITE}/#org` },
    url: `${SITE}/about`,
  },
];
---
<TemplateLayout title="About" description="Jodie built The Digital Income Edit™ backwards, with AI and no face on camera: offer first, audience last. Walk through every room of the real business." schema={schema} stickyHref="/resources/faceless-income-blueprint" stickyLabel="Get the free Blueprint">

<section class="hh">
 <div class="wrap hh-grid ab2-hh">
  <div class="box">
   <span class="stk" style="right:-60px;top:-56px">Hi, I'm<b class="big">Jodie</b></span>
   <svg class="spk" style="left:-26px;bottom:60px;position:absolute"><use href="#sp"/></svg>
   <p class="kick">About the founder</p>
   <h1>I didn't build an audience and then work out <span class="scr">what to sell them.</span></h1>
   <p class="what">I built the business first. The offer, then the funnel, then the automation, and only then the audience, with AI doing the heavy construction and me making every decision. <b>This site is what came out of it, and every room is open.</b></p>
   <a class="btn buy" href="#rooms">Walk through it <span class="ar">→</span></a>
   <p class="see">Jodie, founder of The Digital Income Edit™</p>
  </div>
  <figure class="ab2-fig">
   <div class="hh-ph"><img src="/images/pages/about-porch-red-barn-840.webp" srcset="/images/pages/about-porch-red-barn-560.webp 560w, /images/pages/about-porch-red-barn-840.webp 840w" sizes="(max-width: 820px) 80vw, 360px" width="840" height="1042" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" alt="The brand's AI persona on a weathered farmhouse porch at golden hour, in a cream knit sweater and wool socks, holding a pink mug, with a red barn and open pasture behind her."></div>
   <figcaption class="ab2-cap"><b>Tommy Kate</b>, the brand's AI persona, in her world. My face is never required.</figcaption>
  </figure>
 </div>
</section>

<div class="band"><svg class="spk" style="left:18%"><use href="#sp"/></svg><h2>How I built it</h2><svg class="spk sm" style="right:19%"><use href="#sp"/></svg></div>
<section class="sec wash">
 <div class="wrap">
  <h2 class="h2">Backwards, <span class="scr">on purpose.</span></h2>
  <div class="p44 ab2-built">
   <div class="ph"><img src="/images/pages/about-office-desk-wide-960.webp" srcset="/images/pages/about-office-desk-wide-960.webp 960w, /images/pages/about-office-desk-wide-1600.webp 1600w" sizes="(max-width: 980px) 92vw, 560px" width="1600" height="1073" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="A woman seen from behind at a walnut desk in a sunlit cream study, typing on a laptop beside an open notebook, a brass lamp and white flowers on the built-in shelves."></div>
   <div class="card dash">
    <p><b>I started with no audience and nothing to post. So I started where every other decision gets made: what I'd sell, who it was for and what it would cost her.</b></p>
    <p>Then I built the road a stranger walks from a free guide to a paid one. Then I handed the repeat work to AI and to schedules, so the emails send themselves and one article becomes {weekendEcosystem.assetsPerArticle} finished assets. Only after all of that did I turn on traffic.</p>
    <p>I did it faceless and I did it solo. AI was the build team; I was the architect. The site you're reading, the classroom behind it and the emails that land if you join all came off that one method.</p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

<section class="sec">
 <div class="wrap">
  <p class="kick">What I learned</p>
  <h2 class="h2">Four things the build <span class="scr">taught me.</span></h2>
  <div class="faq">{lessons.map((l, i) => <div class="qa"><span class="n">{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><div><h3>{l.t}</h3><p>{l.p}</p></div></div>)}</div>
 </div>
</section>

<section class="sec wash">
 <div class="wrap">
  <svg class="spk sm" style="right:80px;top:10px"><use href="#sp"/></svg>
  <p class="kick">Why the order matters</p>
  <h2 class="h2">Offer, funnel, automation, <span class="scr">audience last.</span></h2>
  <div class="p18 hm-four">{order.map((o) => <div class="box"><span class="num hm-num">{o.n}</span><h3>{o.name}</h3><p>{o.p}</p></div>)}</div>
  <p class="ab2-hit">Build the rooms in that order and the audience walks into a house that's already finished. That's the whole reason for going backwards.</p>
  <p class="ab2-tag">Build Your Business Backwards. Scale It Forward.™</p>
 </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" id="rooms">
 <div class="wrap">
  <p class="kick">What you can inspect</p>
  <h2 class="h2">Every room <span class="scr">is open.</span></h2>
  <div class="lead"><p>I'm not going to show you screenshots. I'm going to show you the business, and let you walk through it. Open any of these and look at how it was put together.</p></div>
  <div class="ab2-rooms">{inspect.map((r) => <a class="card dash" href={r.href}><span class="hm-lab">{r.room}</span><h3>{r.t}</h3><p>{r.p}</p><span class="btn">{r.go} <span class="ar">→</span></span></a>)}</div>
 </div>
</section>

<section class="sec wash">
 <div class="wrap">
  <div class="p42 dash ab2-next" style="position:relative">
   <span class="stk" style="left:-44px;top:-44px">Free<b class="big">Blueprint</b></span>
   <figure class="card dash ab2-rv">
    <span class="ab2-q" aria-hidden="true">&ldquo;</span>
    <blockquote>{FEATURED.line}</blockquote>
    <figcaption><b>{FEATURED.name}</b>, on {weekendEcosystem.name}</figcaption>
   </figure>
   <div class="tx">
    <p class="kick">Free download</p>
    <h2>See the whole build</h2>
    <span class="scr">on one page.</span>
    <p>The Faceless Income Blueprint™ is free: the whole business, offer to audience, on a single page, and the one room to build first, so the saved tutorials finally turn into something built.</p>
    <a class="btn buy" href="/resources/faceless-income-blueprint">Get the free Blueprint <span class="ar">→</span></a>
    <p class="ab2-alt"><a href={weekendEcosystem.url}>Or build it over one weekend with {weekendEcosystem.name}</a></p>
    <p class="ab2-sign">xoxo, Jodie</p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>
</TemplateLayout>
